@startuml
title Observer / Publish-Subscribe / Listener

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
One-to-many dependency with automatic notifications on state change.

**Motivation**:
GUI event listeners, reactive streams.

**Applicability**:
Event-driven systems; decouple subjects from subscribers.

**Participants**:
Subject maintains observers; observers implement update.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Loose coupling; dynamic subscriptions.
Cons: Notification storms; ordering; memory leaks if not detached.

**Implementation Notes**:
Weak references; event buses; backpressure for reactive streams.

**Known Uses**:
Java PropertyChangeSupport, RxJava/Reactive Streams; GUI listeners.

**Related Patterns**:
Mediator (central coordination), Event Sourcing, Iterator (reactive flows).

endlegend

interface Observer {
  +update(subject: Subject)
}

class ConcreteObserverA
class ConcreteObserverB

interface Subject {
  +attach(obs: Observer)
  +detach(obs: Observer)
  +notifyObservers()
}

class ConcreteSubject {
  -state
}

Observer <|.. ConcreteObserverA
Observer <|.. ConcreteObserverB

Subject <|.. ConcreteSubject
ConcreteSubject o-- Observer : observers
@enduml